# 🛠️ IT Audit Tools

A terminal-based audit toolset built with Python for manual data checking, reconciliation, and summarization.

This app includes:
- 📊 **Anomaly Detection**
  - Manual Entry Detection
  - Improper Description Checker
  - Wrong Account Posting
  - Log Duplication Checker
  - Group Description Sum Checker
- 🔍 **Search Data**
- 🔄 **Reconcile Data**
- 📈 **Summarize Data** (on progress)

---

## 📦 Prerequisites

Before you start, make sure you have the following installed:

| Tool | Description | Install |
|------|-------------|---------|
| 🐍 Python 3.9+ | Required for development (optional for Docker usage) | [python.org](https://www.python.org/) |
| 🐳 Docker | To containerize and run the app | [Install Docker](https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/) |
| 🐙 Git (optional) | To clone the repository | [git-scm.com](https://git-scm.com/) |

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/it-audit-tools.git
cd it-audit-tools
```

### 2. Start with docker 
download docker locally and make a docker account 
and then in the terminal (under the it-audit-tools)

```bash
# Build the image (first time or after updating requirements.txt)
docker compose build

# Run the app
docker compose run --rm audit-tools
```

## Project Structure
```bash
├── main.py                         # Landing menu: Anomalies, Reconcile, Search, Summarize
├── anomalies/
│   ├── anomalies.py               # Submenu for anomaly detection
│   ├── manual_entry.py
│   ├── improper_desc.py
│   ├── account_post.py
│   ├── log_duplication.py
│   └── groupping_desc.py
├── recon.py
├── search.py
├── summarizer.py
├── requirements.txt
├── docker-compose.yml
├── Dockerfile
└── README.md
```


## Clean up cmds
```bash
docker compose down   # Stops containers
docker system prune   # Frees unused Docker space (optional)
```

